    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d608">

                <pb facs="0634" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860D.00/11–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hulley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-29T16:00:00+02:00">November 29,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>734. Opinion in Govt circles is hardening that it will be impossible for
                    Mannerheim to return as President,<anchor n="67" xml:id="d608-f1"/> according to
                    information at Foreign Office. However Mannerheim still takes position that he
                    will return about January 1. Date is significant as under law for trial war
                    responsibles new indictment cannot be filed after end this year. Whether he will
                    return to duty may hinge on how well he recovers health.</p>
                <p>Vuori<anchor n="68" xml:id="d608-f2"/> still leading prospect for Prime Minister.
                    Many think Kukkonen abler but his speeches and writings during Avar are
                    obstacle.</p>
                <p>To Dept as 734 repeated to London as 70.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hulley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d608-f1" n="67" xml:id="d608-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 662, November 6, 1945, 4 p.m., the Chargé in Finland reported that
                    President Mannerheim had left Finland for Portugal, his departure being due to
                    health and political reasons (860D.001/11–645).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d608-f2" n="68" xml:id="d608-f2-content">
                <p>Eero A Wuori (Vuori), Minister of Labor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
